<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Acoma Pueblo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Acoma Pueblo is a Native American pueblo built on a sandstone mesa west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-de-albuquerque">Albuquerque</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a>, and is among the oldest continuously inhabited settlements in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. After its people killed a party of Spanish soldiers in 1598, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-de-onate">Juan de Oñate</a>'s forces stormed the mesa in January 1599, killed several hundred inhabitants and sentenced the survivors to servitude and mutilation. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onati">Oñate</a> was later tried and punished for his conduct.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/acoma-pueblo.jpg" alt="Acoma Pueblo" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Scott Catron · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Acoma_Pueblo_Sky_City_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
